The theme definitions and theme schema are from Pi v1.5.0,
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/tree/f9a26365568127461c47a07a37dcb42c140a3ac5
and are used under its MIT license in PI-LICENSE.

The default coding-assistant preamble, skill guidance and edit/write guidance
in src/resources.rs and src/main.rs are adapted from that same Pi release.

Native terminal-image capability detection and Kitty source-row cropping follow
Pi v1.5.0 terminal-image.ts.
The Rust renderer implements the documented Kitty and iTerm2 protocols.

Markdown heading, fenced code, quote and list presentation in src/ui/render.rs
follows Pi v1.5.0 Markdown rendering conventions.
Edit-diff word highlighting follows Pi v1.5.0 diff.ts presentation conventions.
Edit normalization and unchanged-line preservation in src/text_edit.rs follow
Pi v1.5.0 edit-diff.ts under the same MIT license.

The terminal input decoders adapt Crossterm 0.29.0 (MIT).
See CROSSTERM-LICENSE for its license and copyright notice.

Session search token parsing and fuzzy scoring in src/ui/session_search.rs
adapt Pi v1.5.0 session-selector-search.ts and packages/tui/src/fuzzy.ts.
Session grouping in src/ui/session_threads.rs follows the parent-session tree
and subtree activity ordering in Pi v1.5.0 session-selector.ts.
Resume row layout and relative activity-age units in src/ui/picker.rs follow
Pi v1.5.0 session-selector.ts.

Numbered edit result layout in src/text_edit.rs follows Pi v1.5.0 edit-diff.ts.

Edit matching diagnostics in src/text_edit.rs follow Pi v1.5.0 edit-diff.ts.

Model scope resolution in src/model_selection.rs follows Pi v1.5.0 model-resolver.ts.
